            <ArticleTitle>Acute bacterial thyroiditis presenting as otalgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>788-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of acute bacterial thyroiditis due to Haemophilus influenzae infection presenting as otalgia is reported. The features of this condition and the differential diagnosis from subacute (DeQuervains) thyroiditis are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
